  "geometryBasis": "The named temple ring and adjoining building ring fix the plan at Dantewada. The Chhattisgarh Culture Department records the matching coordinates 18°53′48″N, 81°20′42″E. The historic sculptures site at Barsoor has a separate official listing.",
  "sectionBasis": "The Archaeological Survey counted nine stepped courses on the east-facing sanctuary and documented the pillared and tiled halls and Garuda pillar. Exact 2022 CC0 originals establish the surviving timber screen, whitewashed pyramidal profiles and red plinth accents.",
  "limitations": [
    "The model represents the main historic temple and adjoining shrine. The distant three-arch road gateway and temporary visitor facilities are outside this footprint.",
    "The named rings bind the walls. Metrical heights, inner bay divisions, plinth elevation and the height of the adjoining white shrine are estimated from the public-domain photographs and architectural survey.",
    "The Garuda pillar top and historic ornament are simplified. Contemporary printed signs, ropes and movable objects are omitted."
